


## v2 build / deploy (src/)

Dev (readable modules, COOP/COEP):
```
cd src
npm install
npm run serve
```
Open http://localhost:5173 — edit app/ sim/ render/, refresh. No rebuild.

Optional vendor rebuilds (only when those deps change — not every edit):
```
npm run build:lite
npm run build:explorer
npm run build:howler
```

Prebake (VAT dumps, mesh packages with materials, spawn/FX sockets → ../assets/baked/).
Needs Chrome + WebGPU. Speeds up both local serve and prod:
```
npm run prebake
```
Re-run when models / VAT clips change. Serve and package both use assets/baked/ when present.
Static meshes load bake geo+materials (no GLB parse); villager VAT still needs its GLB for skinning.

Package upload folder:
```
npm run package
```
Fills ../DEPLOY/ (index at root, hashed+minified JS, assets incl. baked, PWA).
JS is two bundles (main + worker) — not hundreds of Lite chunks.
Obfuscation off by default; opt-in: PACKAGE_OBFUSCATE=1 (main + sim worker — both are fully bundled).
Do not open index.html from disk (file:// / CORS / SAB).

To deploy:
 - Upload the *contents* of DEPLOY/ to the S3 bucket root (not the DEPLOY folder name)
 - CloudFront → Distributions → Invalidation "/*"
 - CloudFront MUST send these on HTML (ideally all responses) or the game stays a black/fallback screen:
     Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
     Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
   (Response headers policy on the distribution. Without them SharedArrayBuffer is undefined
   and crossOriginIsolated is false — check console: window.crossOriginIsolated)







The Bitmask Logic:
Bit 0 (North): Set if North neighbor is different
Bit 1 (East): Set if East neighbor is different
Bit 2 (South): Set if South neighbor is different
Bit 3 (West): Set if West neighbor is different
